    "_why_two_references": "Linearising about a CONSTANT Q makes the quasi-steady Jacobian nearly rank one, and that is not an artefact: with Mdot_p tied to Q and the total mass fixed, every node sits at the same flux, so all 12 perturbation directions differ only by the time-weight of their basis function.  That degeneracy is Theorem 1 showing up numerically.  It would, however, flatter the front-limited model, so the comparison is repeated about a waning reference, where the quasi-steady map has genuine structure and the difference measures what the front actually adds."
